## Changes made

```tsx
export default defineApp([
  setCommonHeaders(),
  ({ ctx }) => {
    // setup ctx here
    ctx;
  },
  // /status returns a raw JSON Response (does not need the Document wrapper)
  route("/status", () => {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ ok: true, name: "rwsdk" }), {
      headers: { "content-type": "application/json" },
    });
  }),
  render(Document, [
    route("/", Home),
    route("/ping", () => {
      return <h1>Pong!</h1>;
    }),
    route("/about", () => {
      return (
        <>
          <h1>About RedwoodSDK</h1>
          <p>React framework for Cloudflare.</p>
        </>
      );
    }),
    route("/greet/:name", ({ params }) => {
      return <h1>Hello, {params.name}!</h1>;
    }),
  ]),
]);
```

## Verification

I started the dev server (`npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173`) and tested each route with `curl`:

| Route | Result |
|-------|--------|
| `GET /ping` | Full HTML document containing `<h1>Pong!</h1>` ✓ |
| `GET /about` | Full HTML document containing `<h1>About RedwoodSDK</h1>` and `<p>React framework for Cloudflare.</p>` ✓ |
| `GET /status` | Raw JSON: `{"ok":true,"name":"rwsdk"}` (no Document wrapper) ✓ |
| `GET /greet/world` | Full HTML document containing `<h1>Hello, world!</h1>` ✓ |

### Key implementation notes
- **`/status`** is placed *outside* the `render(Document, [...])` block since it returns a raw `Response` object (not JSX), per the requirement.
- **`/ping`, `/about`, and `/greet/:name`** live inside `render(Document, [...])` so they return full HTML pages wrapped by the `Document` component.
- **`/greet/:name`** uses the route's path parameter via `({ params }) => ...` and interpolates `params.name` into the JSX, so `/greet/world` renders `Hello, world!`. (React inserts HTML comment markers `<!-- -->` around the dynamic value, which is normal SSR behavior and the rendered text still reads `Hello, world!`.)
